### Bot AI detailed implementation

Coordinate system: world/local group of course. start z=8, finish negative. Player uses pos.z decreasing. Bots should start on start platform at z ~ 8.9 lane offsets. `b.z` initial startZ.

Each bot:
- `progress` derived: `(startZ - z)/totalDistance`.
- `baseSpeed`: totalDistance / finishTime (finishTime computed as par * factor).
- `speedMul` computed per frame from rubber band & skill.
- `z -= speed * dt` (forward).
- `x`: lateral velocity `vx` integrated; target lane from AI.
- `y`: vertical integrated.

Lane range: need course width at current position. `course.groundAt(x, z, ...)` returns platform. We can get `platform.w` and `platform.x`, but for discs contains uses radius. For lane candidates, use fixed range [-7,7] with maybe current platform. Simpler: use `const halfW = groundInfo?.platform?.w ? Math.min(8, groundInfo.platform.w/2) : 7;` But at beams (w 4.6) width half 2.3. Candidate lanes must stay on beam. So candidates = fractions of halfW minus margin. Use platform width. If not grounded/no platform, use last known halfW (b.halfW) default 6.

Compute danger using `course.hitObstacle({x:cx, y:b.y, z: probeZ}, 0.5, 1.5)`. For sweeper hit depends on its angle (updated). Good.

